jt-pve-storage-purestorage (1.1.11-1) stable; urgency=high

  * [HIGH] Volume create/clone in a pod with any policy attached failed
    with "Pod contains file systems or policies." (context: <podname>),
    blocking VM disk creation entirely. Field reproducer: a Pure storage
    configured with --pure-pod pvepod2 where the operator had attached a
    quota policy 'pvepodquota2' via Storage > Policies in the GUI; every
    'qm create' that needed a disk failed at PureStoragePlugin.pm:1660
    inside alloc_image's volume_create call. Root cause: per the FA 2.26
    OpenAPI spec, POST /volumes (and POST /volumes for clones) defaults
    to with_default_protection=true, which causes Pure to apply the
    pod's container default protection to the new volume. Pure rejects
    that step when the pod has policies attached (the quota policy
    counts), surfacing the misleading "Pod contains file systems or
    policies." error. Fixed by passing with_default_protection=false on
    the POST /volumes call when the volume name carries a "pod::"
    prefix, both in volume_create and volume_clone. The PVE plugin does
    not rely on Pure's default protection (it manages snapshots itself
    via volume_snapshot/volume_overwrite), so this is the correct
    semantic. Non-pod volumes are left untouched to preserve any
    user-configured array-level default_protections.

